Nancy Lebovitz comments on the inferiority of automated massage

[...]

A friend of mine has for about five years had a rather expensive massage
chair manufactured by -- I think -- Panasonic.  I'm not a regular recipient
of massage from humans, so I can't do a real comparison, but in absolute
terms, the chair is good enough that I enjoy sitting in it for half an hour
or more, and when it's time to get up I am so relaxed that it is difficult
to do so.

The chair has two massage heads (possibly rollers or casters of some sort)
that move about under the back panel - that which supports you from lower
hips to neck as you recline.  They work in and out from positions just
